==Battleground==
*1 [[Metal Cyclone]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*3 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*10 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 116.67 seconds<sup>3,500f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*10 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
An incredibly efficient way to beat this level is to spam [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasauruses]] and [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Showoff Cats]]; the large amount of Showoff Cats should constantly freeze Metal Cyclone while the Catasauruses keep doing [[Critical Hit]]s and finish off Metal Cyclone. Make sure to use the other slots for the [[Space is the Place (Insane)|second stage]]. If you don't have Catasaurus, you can replace it with [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] and optionally one other [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critter]].

==Trivia==
*Nuts 'n' Bolts' Japanese name, Kiki Kaikai (機々械々), is a pun on the idiom "Kiki Kaikai" (奇々怪々), meaning "extremely bizarre". The joke is that the kanji used for the stage name share the same pronunciations as those in the idiom but have entirely different meanings; in English, it would mean something like "extremely machined" or "extremely mechanical".
**In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], this pun was reused for the description of [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%C9%A5%ED%A5%BF%A5%DC%A1%BC%A5%B0Dk-2 Dorotaborg Dk-2] ([[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Dorotabō|Dorotabō]]'s Serious/Metal variant), which combined the two aforementioned spellings of "Kiki Kaikai" into one: 奇機怪械.

